--- !u!114 &1709852095
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1709852081}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 40fe67fde4a4351409089804b4848b92, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _documentationText: 'MediaPipe Hand Landmarker Example

    Detects hands and 21
    hand landmarks per hand from input frames with optional 3D skeleton visualization.



    Demonstrates:

    -
    Reading input frames via MultiSourceToMatHelper (webcam, video file, image file,
    or GPU readback)

    - Loading palm detection and hand landmark ONNX/Sentis
    models from StreamingAssets

    - Toggling Sentis vs OpenCV DNN inference and
    optional async detection

    - Converting RGBA frames to BGR, running MediaPipeHandLandmarkerMultiBackend,
    and visualizing landmarks on Mat



    OpenCV classes and APIs used:

    -
    Mat, Size, Scalar, Point

    - Imgproc: cvtColor

    - MediaPipeHandLandmarkerMultiBackend,
    MatSingleFlightSyncAsyncRunner, MultiBackendDnn

    - MultiSourceToMatHelper,
    OpenCVMatUnityUtils



    Referring to:

    https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe



    [Tested
    Models]

    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EnoxSoftware/OpenCVForUnityExampleAssets/f4f791d5f330cdef388369f78120457f23f8998d/dnn/MediaPipeHandLandmarkerExample/hand_detector.onnx

    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EnoxSoftware/OpenCVForUnityExampleAssets/f4f791d5f330cdef388369f78120457f23f8998d/dnn/MediaPipeHandLandmarkerExample/hand_landmarks_detector.onnx'
  AlignmentSetting: 0
